+#1 particle diameter is avg(29.5/27, 73/64)" =avg(1.0926, 1.1406)" = 1.1166"
+#horizontal divider for spacing closer together is 1.1406/1.0926 = 1.0440
+    #as a result of this division, we can get the scalings.
+    #a scale of 94.5 on the pvc cylinder is all 64 vertical (head to toe) taxels.
+    #in the real world, a 24" pipe covers 24/1.1406 = 21.04 taxels.
+    #thus the scale needs to be 94.5*(21.04/64) = 31.07
+
+    #a scale of 55.0 on a square spans 37 vertical (head to toe) taxels.
+    #in the real world, a 11.75" square covers 11.75/1.1406 = 10.30 taxels
+    #thus the scale needs to be 55*(10.30/36.5) = 15.523
+
+
+To convert meters to FleX units (fx):
+Each particle is 0.075 fx wide.
+The distance between top of bed and bottom of bed is 64 particles.
+From top to bottom measured from particle centers, length of bed is 0.075*64  = 4.8 fx.
+Vertical taxels on the bed are 1.1406" apart. 
+Thus top to bottom distance is 1.1406*64 = 73" or 1.8542 m.
+Thus right to left distance is 1.0926*27 = 29.5" or 0.7493 m.
+Conversion from meters to fx: (4.8 fx/ 1.8542m) = 2.58872 fx/m.
+
+center of the mattress is:
+	bottom of top (of person): 1.8542*2.58872/2 = 2.40000
+	right to left (of person): 0.7493*2.58872/2 = 0.96986
+	
+	
+	
+To calculate distance from each force to the nearest capsule to find the capsule it applies to:
+
+Get set of endpoints and radii defining each capsule
+For each force location:
+	Calculate distance to center of all capsules
+	Pick 5 closest capsules
+	For each capsule in [5 closest capsules]:
+		Pick end sphere at random
+		Calculate distance d1 to center of sphere
+		Put point tiny step close to the other end of the capsule
+		Calculate distance d2 to this point
+		if d1 is less:
+			D = d1 - r_capsule
+			else:
+				Pick other end sphere
+				Calculate distance d3 to center of other sphere
+				Put point tiny step closer to other end
+				Calculate distance d4 to this point
+				if d3 is less:
+					D = d3 - r_capsule
+				else:
+					find point p2 on line d1 -> d4 closest to p
+					D = |p2 - p1| - r_capsule
+	Pick the capsule out of the 5 that has the lowest value of D and store it with the force vector.
